# Infinity Radius FreeRADIUS dictionary.
#
# Pulls in FreeRADIUS's own stock dictionary (which defines the standard
# RFC 2865/2866 attributes: Session-Timeout, Idle-Timeout, ...) plus the
# MikroTik vendor dictionary (Mikrotik-Rate-Limit and the rest of vendor
# 14988's attributes) that ships with every FreeRADIUS install — neither is
# hand-authored here, since redefining a vendor attribute's number incorrectly
# would silently corrupt what's sent to routers.
#
# On a stock Debian/Ubuntu FreeRADIUS install these live in
# /usr/share/freeradius/ — a bare `$INCLUDE dictionary.mikrotik` resolves
# relative to this file's own directory (/etc/freeradius/3.0), NOT the
# dictionary search path, so it must be the full path (confirmed against a
# real FreeRADIUS 3.2.5 install on Ubuntu 24.04 — the short form fails with
# "Couldn't open dictionary ... No such file or directory").

$INCLUDE /usr/share/freeradius/dictionary
$INCLUDE /usr/share/freeradius/dictionary.mikrotik
